# Clients synced from the PacketFence server.
#
# The sync-radius-nas oneshot writes one client file per switch into this
# directory at container start, before radiusd-auth starts (s6 dependency),
# so the files are included statically here.
#
# The FreeRADIUS dynamic-clients "directory" mechanism cannot be used for
# these: it resolves an unknown source by reading the file named after the
# packet's source IP, which can never match a subnet-keyed switch (e.g.
# 192.168.1.0/24). Static client blocks support a CIDR ipaddr and FreeRADIUS
# picks overlapping clients by longest prefix, so a single-IP switch inside
# a subnet switch still wins with its own secret.
#
# Clients refresh on container restart, exactly like before: the previous
# dynamic directory's files were only ever written at container start too.
$INCLUDE ${confdir}/dynamic-clients/
